ifa/issues/102 (was 030) -- `if root.parts:` truth-tests a {list, tuple} union (a tuple field later reassigned list+tuple), which has no runtime dispatch: C aborts with "matching function not found" and LLVM segfaults. This test had no check file, so it passed as compile-only while aborting on both backends (found by ifa/181's IFA_DBG_NOEMIT census). The check file holds CPython's output and this flips to PASS when the union dispatches.
